### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@paymentIntentId = 1a5f97cb-4c2d-4078-8f6e-bb12c60c5b70

### 0. Login to get token (run this first, or whenever token expires)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "duplicate-test@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("authToken", response.body.token);
%}

### 1. CREATE — first-time request with a brand new idempotency key
# Expect: 202 Accepted, a real PaymentIntent body (status = CREATED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 1999,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 2. DUPLICATE_COMPLETE — replay the exact same request
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: fixed-test-key-0001
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 2500,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 3. Validation failure — missing/invalid amount
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 0,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 4. Validation failure — missing currency
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 1500
}

### 5. Missing Idempotency-Key header entirely
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 1500,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 6. Different currency — JPY
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 500,
  "currency": "JPY"
}

### 7. DUPLICATE_PENDING (manual/concurrency test, placeholder)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: concurrency-test-key-0001
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 3000,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 8. PROCESS — transition a payment intent from CREATED to SUCCEEDED
# Replace {{paymentIntentId}} with a real id from a prior CREATE response (must currently be CREATED).
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/process
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 9. PROCESS — invalid transition (double-process the same id)
# Expect: 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/process
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 10. PROCESS — nonexistent id
# Expect: 404 Not Found
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/process
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ============================================
### Ownership tests — cross-merchant access
### ============================================

### 11. Login as a SECOND, different merchant
# Register this account first if it doesn't already exist.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "merchant-test@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("otherMerchantToken", response.body.token);
%}

### 12. OTHER merchant tries to process merchant A's payment intent
# Use a paymentIntentId that belongs to the FIRST merchant (from request 1's response), currently CREATED.
# Expect: 404 Not Found — ownership check should hide existence, not leak a 403.
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/process
Authorization: Bearer {{otherMerchantToken}}